<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39862" root="نصب" body-key="n">
    
      8 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انتصب</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تنصّب</span></b> , quasi-pass. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَصَبَ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَصَّبَ</span>, <i>He,</i> or <i>it, became set up, put up, set
upright,</i> or <i>erected; stood up,</i> or <i>upright,</i> or <i>erect;
became elevated, raised,</i> or <i>reared:</i> (K:) <i>became
even and erect.</i> (TA, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نص</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>He stood
erect, raising his head.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [<i>It was,</i> or
<i>became, erect, vertical,</i> or <i>perpendicular.</i>] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4- 
[<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انتصب شَعَرُهُ</span> <i>His hair, being full-grown, stood
out:</i> see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنْتَصِبٌ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انتصب</span> (TA) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تنصّب</span></b> 
(K) (tropical:)  <i>It</i> (dust) <i>rose high.</i> (K, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b6-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنْتَصِبْ</span>
<i>Set up thy cooking-pot</i> [<i>upon the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِنْصَب</span>, or <i>trivet,</i>]
<i>to cook,</i> said to a cook. (IAar.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b7-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انتصبت</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْنَانُهُ إِلَى قُدَّامٍ</span> [<i>Its teeth stood out forwards:</i>
see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنْتَصِبٌ</span>:] said of a mouth. (TA, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دفق</span>.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b8-  [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِنْتِصَابٌ</span> is often used absolutely as meaning
<i>An erection of the penis.</i>] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b9-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">انتصب الحَرْفُ</span> <i>The
letter</i> [meaning the final letter of a word] <i>was
written,</i> or <i>pronounced,</i> with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَصْب</span>: [see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَصَبَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحَرْفَ</span>]. (S.)

